{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1453812-tresse-in-the-cod","id":1453812,"title":"Tresse in the CoD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-06-29T21:16:16-07:00","id":1453812,"title":"Tresse in the CoD","content":"So, I just got done watching Trese on Netflix, and I couldn't help but feel that this show fits just so neatly in the Chronicles of Darkness, and started thinking of how one could use CoD venues to make a homebrew Trese game, or at least a Trese-inspired CoD game set in Manilla using one or more of the venues.<br /> <br /> The Lakon seem like they are very obvious Mages, and the ritual where she enters the Giant Tree (I forget its name) and comes back five years later with access to magic could easily be an Awakening ritual where members of the Trese family write their name on the tower of Moros. The Lakon could even be their own particular Legacy. They don't seem to fit neatly into one Order though. I'd be tempted to say Adamantine Arrow because of how bold and warrior like they are.<br /> <br /> The Aswang seem like Vampires mainly of the Gangrel and Deva clans operating together in Manilla. Given the setting and style, I'd say they belong to Circle of the Crone.<br /> <br /> The rest of the various creatures from Philippine folklore in Trese could easily be pulled from Changeling: the Lost. Straight up. The Tikbalang, the Wind People, the Mushroom guys, Nuno the goblin informant in the sewer, the lightning god who runs the power company, the Tiyanak, etc. They're all either True Fae, goblins, or courts of Changelings working with the Lakon mages to maintain some kind of balance in Manilla. Datu Talagbusao, the main villain, would be a True Fae without question (except for the fact that he had kids, but maybe he just took his worshipper's twin boys to his demense and raised them as his own?). Nuno might be from the Goblin Market, and sells information.<br /> <br /> The Tiyanak, instead of being some version of Changeling, might be a misbegotten child Promethian, and exist as a cautionary tale as to why the main types of Promethians don't make children versions of themselves.<br /> <br /> There are of course ghosts in the series, and those are in every venue. Ibu, however, might be a Geist that guides the dead to the underworld.<br /> <br /> While werewolves are briefly seen in the series, more prominently shown are Spirits like the ones detailed in Werewolf: the Forsaken. The fire spirit that resides in Alexandra's phone which she periodically calls upon for aid is a prime example of such a spirit.<br /> <br /> What do you think? How would you flesh out a Trese inspired game using CoD venues? Would you try to work in other venues, or restrict your Manilla setting to one venue like Mage or Changeling?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10065,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10065-zolace","user":"Zolace","date":". One S. 07-03-2021, 07:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10065-zolace","name":"Zolace","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T06:55:53-07:00","id":1453928,"title":"","content":"For the Aswang, there are three breeds detailed in &quot;Night Horrors: the Wicked Dead&quot;. I think they are even usable in second edition without great problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/422-lykas","name":"Lykas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar422_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"}